{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1213","id":4974193763,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUoK9js8AAAABKHwsYw","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1213","diff_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1213.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1213.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1213","number":1213,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"T-2794: replace parked carriage and refine wagon finishes","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Replaces the obsolete unoccupied C02 display in the 1904 Prairie scene with the catalogue-guided Brougham at its already qualified curbside stop. The 1893 Studebaker catalogue identifies a design; this Chicago specimen, owner and stop remain reconstructed. The C02 definition/assets remain available, all five distinct 1835 wagon placements remain, and the Brougham position/bearing stay fixed.\n\nThe exact 33,502-triangle near delivery, articulation anchors, contacts and original conservative collision proxy are preserved. The independently checked distance model now uses 11,706 triangles with the same physical feature categories, seven materials and existing 24 m selector. The three W01 farm-box wagons gain reviewed modern Poly Haven CC0 wood texture maps with GPL project charts; their original geometry/paint/iron and baseline asset remain. The two distinct covered wagons receive the exact saved cloth-drape refinement while retaining their separate finishes, seeds, yokes, stands and newer terrain evidence. Modern texture maps do not attest historical species, finish, specimen or photographic capture method.\n\nIncorporates reviewed dev `5135fb76`, preserving its complete Inspect/Research UI changes and tracked Ames roof refinement as well as the earlier Glessner recourse. The smoke retains independent full initial-Welcome and Home-Confidence tap contracts and all 222 actual 1904 structures; the 27 previously missing Indiana IDs precede the unchanged incoming 195-ID body. Cameras, tiers, limits, timeouts, confidence and other incoming guards are unchanged. The optional Full shadow-culler flag remains off.\n\nThe first actual newer-runtime GitHub test merge (run39906632536, checkout36546dcf, parents[a3,133]) failed only the legacy popup HTML hash contract. Exact upstream513 popup/import modules and its own adapter independently rendered the frozen six legacy inputs. The old133 closure first reproduced every stored original hash; upstream513 and the feature adapter then produced byte-identical new cards and HTML. All six outputs differ only in line-leading indentation (38 fewer bytes each), from upstream's research-pane factoring. Only six raw HTML hashes and explicit provenance changed. All card JSON hashes, openings, design hashes, source assertions and four semantic negative controls remain unchanged; the original full card+native-LOD test passed. The failed CI run remains recorded.\n\nValidation for `a22ca758323e6e2f1ed9f3909a88fb98636be55c` / tree `fa427eb201de4bad4b7265313fcc5a422f440ea4`: full preflight passed 1,052 steps (382 self-tests), changelog and ID checks in 688.517 seconds. Authored-candidate and actual committed-head changelog/ID/whitespace checks passed. Normal postcommit publication, complete mirror check and published-site validation passed; build `a22ca7583`, 2026-10-23T06:45:00Z. The normal branch push is confirmed at this exact merge commit with parents `133754065` and `5135fb76`.\n\nBefore the full gate, all nine focused checks passed: original full card+LOD, exact near/mid/proxy, placement identity, parameters/licenses/freshness, liberties compiler, syntax, whitespace and changelog. Protected proof preserves 57 of the 63 vehicle-PR paths byte-for-byte at133, all 17 transport GLBs/near sidecar, and every nonshared incoming513 path. The other five paths are normal shared merges; the sixth intentional difference is the independently derived fixture. Incoming UI/Ames and both sets of liberty edits are preserved. No broad rebuild was needed. Fresh normal CI and source-bound world review remain pending.\n\nThe first dev513 preflight was run in restricted execution mode and failed 30/1,052 steps plus its changelog subprocess check; one fallback-summary stdin stall required stopping only its owned Node/Python processes, including the canonical harness automatic retry. The unchanged fallback test then passed in 0.317 seconds with the same interpreter under elevated execution. This historical failed gate remains recorded separately from the corrected full-gate result above.\n\nThe first combined full gate failed only on three missing explicit asset-license registry paths. Exact registration rows corrected that ledger without changing the validator or GPL-project/CC0-pixel attribution. Earlier native/mobile and world-deadline failures remain failures. The optional culler experiment retained one equal RGBA cell but failed overall on four aborted requests; two cells were not run and the flag remains off.\n\nRoot accepted eight fixed 24 m near/mid views for distance LOD only and four W01 material views for a bounded improvement. Saved cloth-source qualification is historical, not qualification of this combined integration. The earlier staged c9cd75af Full-OFF spawn reading was 4,596,121/4,600,000 triangles and 4,668/7,800 draws; the carriage is outside that frame. This does not establish current close vehicle appearance, world clearance or photographic completion.\n\nDraft remains open pending fresh normal CI, source-bound normal desktop/mobile world review and photographic acceptance. People/horse occupants, coupling, driving, boarding, riding and parent-ticket completion are not claimed.\n\nSuperseded by merged PR #1175 (DEV commit fffae74c728b469163d3c1a6997aea29b4b9b7b3, tree 1d6048e957bfca326db1cdd0aecd16e62f1bd96a). The combined delivery passed its actual full preflight and fresh normal GitHub checks. A strict comparison accounts for all 63 original paths: 53 exact files/deletion, 9 explicitly verified shared unions/canonical outputs and the four vehicle changelog items transferred unchanged to the combined entry. All 695 original liberty records and the 222 smoke structure IDs remain. Closing this duplicate PR preserves its history; photographic finishing, horses, occupants, teams and riding/boarding remain open in their tickets.\n","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:12:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T10:11:58Z","closed_at":"2026-10-23T10:11:57Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1213/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1213/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1213/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chic